        "question": {
          ":question/id": "601674d8-aea4-509a-a683-3af0e8f4e5ad",
          ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
          ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/generate/scratch/17592186124473/plots/plot-fdfe2b78989797aae40a1f3f3e0c2b1bf0e520c800951ac6334fc3c4d35e11da.png)\n\nWhich listed domain retains every input outside the constant segment and is maximal by inclusion among the listed domains on which $f(x)$ is invertible?",
          ":question/worked-solution": "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n- On $x\\in [1,4]$ the graph is constant, so we can retain only one point at output $y=0$.\n\n- On $x\\in [-2,1]\\cup (4,6]$ the left piece has output at most zero and the right piece has output greater than zero. Each piece is one-to-one, and their ranges do not overlap.\n\n- Adding any excluded plateau point repeats the output zero. Every other listed domain either omits a nonconstant piece or fails the horizontal line test.\n\nTherefore, the correct listed domain is:\n\n$$\nx\\in [-2,1]\\cup (4,6]\n$$",
